Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 (touches no file of patches 0001-0012).
A remote MessageQueue reader busy-polls before sleeping (VLLM_MQ_REMOTE_SPIN_MS, e.g. 200; 0 = off, the default). With
tensor parallelism across nodes (--nnodes 2, the headless rank on the second Spark), each step's scheduler output
reaches the remote worker over a ZMQ socket, and MessageQueue.recv sleeps in zmq's poll until it arrives, while the
head node's local worker spins on shared memory. A thread woken from an idle GB10 core starts ~0.4 ms late
(TensorFold measured 433 us, and cut its follower's first-gather wait from 440 to 26 us by busy polling: github.com/
bertholomus/TensorFold, branch deepseek-v41-tp2, 8ec371c / 7e2bc6f), and every rank then waits for the late one at
the step's first all-reduce: in our k=3 profile the embedding's all-reduce absorbed a 272 / 341 us start skew twice a
step (LOG Oct 10 21:28, scripts/bench/trace_gaps.py). With the knob set, the remote reader polls without sleeping for
that many milliseconds after each message, then falls back to the blocking poll with the same timeout, so decode steps
(tens of ms apart) never sleep and an idle server does not burn a core.

diff --git a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/shm_broadcast.py b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/shm_broadcast.py
index bafc572..07736bc 100644
--- a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/shm_broadcast.py
+++ b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/shm_broadcast.py
@@ -61,6 +61,11 @@ if TYPE_CHECKING:
     from _typeshed import SizedBuffer
 
 VLLM_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL = envs.VLLM_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL
+# A remote reader (a worker on another node) busy-polls its socket for this long after each message before it falls
+# back to sleeping in zmq's poll; 0 (default) keeps the plain blocking poll. A thread woken from an idle core starts
+# late (~0.4 ms on GB10), and with tensor parallelism across nodes every other rank then waits for it at the step's
+# first collective; decode steps arrive well inside the window, an idle server still sleeps.
+REMOTE_SPIN_SECONDS = float(os.environ.get("VLLM_MQ_REMOTE_SPIN_MS", "0") or 0) / 1000
 # Cap on how long an idle reader parks before re-reading the authoritative SHM
 # written-flag. Bounds lost-notify recovery latency to ~5s while the periodic
 # wakeup stays negligible (one flag check per reader every 5s).
@@ -912,7 +917,10 @@ class MessageQueue:
             if overflow:
                 obj = MessageQueue.recv(self.local_socket, timeout)
         elif self._is_remote_reader:
-            obj = MessageQueue.recv(self.remote_socket, timeout)
+            if REMOTE_SPIN_SECONDS > 0:
+                obj = MessageQueue.recv_spin(self.remote_socket, timeout, REMOTE_SPIN_SECONDS)
+            else:
+                obj = MessageQueue.recv(self.remote_socket, timeout)
         else:
             raise RuntimeError("Only readers can dequeue")
         return obj
@@ -926,6 +934,20 @@ class MessageQueue:
         recv, *recv_oob = socket.recv_multipart(copy=False)
         return pickle.loads(recv, buffers=recv_oob)
 
+    @staticmethod
+    def recv_spin(socket: zmq.Socket, timeout: float | None, spin: float) -> Any:
+        """recv(), polling without sleeping for up to `spin` seconds before the blocking poll (the same timeout)."""
+        start = time.monotonic()
+        while not socket.poll(timeout=0):
+            elapsed = time.monotonic() - start
+            if timeout is not None and elapsed >= timeout:
+                raise TimeoutError
+            if elapsed >= spin:
+                left = None if timeout is None else max(0.0, timeout - elapsed)
+                return MessageQueue.recv(socket, left)
+        recv, *recv_oob = socket.recv_multipart(copy=False)
+        return pickle.loads(recv, buffers=recv_oob)
+
     def broadcast_object(self, obj=None):
         if self._is_writer:
             self.enqueue(obj)
